.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BIO_SOCKET_WAIT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BIO_socket_wait ,
.Nm BIO_wait ,
.Nm BIO_do_connect_retry
.Nd BIO connection utility functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bio.h
.Fd #ifndef OPENSSL_NO_SOCK
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_socket_wait
.Fa "int fd"
.Fa "int for_read"
.Fa "time_t max_time"
.Fc
.Fd #endif
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_wait
.Fa "BIO *bio"
.Fa "time_t max_time"
.Fa "unsigned int nap_milliseconds"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_do_connect_retry
.Fa "BIO *bio"
.Fa "int timeout"
.Fa "int nap_milliseconds"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn BIO_socket_wait
waits on the socket
.Fa fd
for reading if
.Fa for_read
is not 0, else for writing, at most until
.Fa max_time .
It succeeds immediately if
.Fa max_time
== 0 (which means no timeout given).
.Pp
.Fn BIO_wait
waits at most until
.Fa max_time
on the given (typically socket-based)
.Fa bio ,
for reading if
.Fa bio
is supposed to read, else for writing.
It is used by
.Fn BIO_do_connect_retry
and can be used together
.Xr BIO_read 3 .
It succeeds immediately if
.Fa max_time
== 0 (which means no timeout given).
If sockets are not available it supports polling by succeeding after
sleeping at most the given
.Fa nap_milliseconds
in order to avoid a tight busy loop.
Via
.Fa nap_milliseconds
the caller determines the polling granularity.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_do_connect_retry
connects via the given
.Fa bio .
It retries
.Xr BIO_do_connect 3
as far as needed to reach a definite outcome, i.e., connection
succeeded, timeout has been reached, or an error occurred.
For nonblocking and potentially even non-socket BIOs it polls every
.Fa nap_milliseconds
and sleeps in between using
.Fn BIO_wait .
If
.Fa nap_milliseconds
is < 0 then a default value of 100 ms is used.
If the
.Fa timeout
parameter is > 0 this indicates the maximum number of seconds to wait
until the connection is established or a definite error occurred.
A value of 0 enables waiting indefinitely (i.e, no timeout), while a
value < 0 means that
.Xr BIO_do_connect 3
is tried only once.
The function may, directly or indirectly, invoke
.Xr ERR_clear_error 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BIO_socket_wait ,
.Fn BIO_wait ,
and
.Fn BIO_do_connect_retry
return -1 on error, 0 on timeout, and 1 on success.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BIO_do_connect 3 ,
.Xr BIO_read 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn BIO_socket_wait ,
.Fn BIO_wait ,
and
.Fn BIO_do_connect_retry
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
